THE ENERGY BASIS OF LAYER 3'S DECISIONS L3-OD1, L3-OD2 AND L3-OD4 (energy_basis.py second issue, stream l3plane,
MESHSAT-1357). PROTOTYPE DESIGN: nothing built, powered or measured. Energy figures MODELED (a1elec's energy_two_pack.py,
pinned, as reconcile_lid_panel.py runs it); the bus range from vbus20_range.py (MAKER, NETLIST, INFERRED per term); bands
and thresholds INFERRED from the model's grid. The author's analysis, AI arithmetic; not a qualified review, and not
the independent check.

0. REPRODUCTION
   0a. v2/docs/records/a1int/reconcile_lid_panel.out: 21 of 21 rows reproduced byte for byte by this script's runs at 20.7 V
   0b. U3's day at E2 (20.7 V, 6.2 A): 0.9722 / 0.9790 / 0.9826, equal to efficiency.py's daily() and to v2/docs/records/s117/efficiency.out section 7 (yes)
   0c. v2/docs/records/l3plane/plane_grid.out case P (6.1 A, U3B carried, 20.7 V): 100 of 100 plane cells (both lid options, both array builds) reproduced
   0d. the mean day fed as a 72 hour series reproduces the mean-day runs exactly (both lids, both starts): yes
   0e. the first issue's WE (case WE1 here) reproduces its six rows of v2/docs/records/l3plane/energy_basis.out at 6a283b25: yes

1. THE CASES, EXACTLY
   1a. THE WEATHER: SC-37's reference day, the only weather these runs establish
       resource: PVGIS 5.2, PVGIS-SARAH2 monthly means 2015 to 2020 at latitude 52.160, longitude 4.497 (v2/vendor/solar/pvgis-leiden-monthly-2015-2020.json), the September mean day
       on the 40 degree, azimuth 0 plane (PVGIS's optimum): 4.014 kWh/m2 a day
       shape: PVGIS DRcalc's September mean-day profile, PVGIS-SARAH2 2005 to 2020, hourly, UTC, on that plane (v2/docs/records/a1solar/inputs/pvgis-leiden-daily-profile-2005-2020.json: 3.983 kWh/m2),
       scaled by 1.007820 to the monthly mean; the same 24 hours repeated for 72 hours; runs from 06 and 18 UTC, a full pack;
       air 13.23 to 18.33 C (the profile's T2m), the lid pack at 13.23 C (its minimum) and the base pack at +20 C for 72 hours.
       Other planes: each plane's own DRcalc mean day (v2/vendor/solar/pvgis-planes/), scaled by the same factor.
       NO WORSE-WEATHER CASE IS ESTABLISHED BY THESE RUNS: a mean day is not a cloudy day; section 7 is INFORMATIVE only.
   1b. THE ARRAY BUILD (both on the SAME mean day; the ratio multiplies PVGIS's 0.9417, the 40/0 plane's losses kept for every plane)
       TYP, the typical build: fit 'Rs 0 (section 3)', the FBIN point at 34.29 V, NOCT 45 C, a 5 m lead (0.0465 ohm loop).
       WAB, the WORST ARRAY BUILD (the earlier records' case C, renamed; it is NOT weather): the worst of the three single-diode
       fits (Rs 0 (section 3), Rs 0.1, Rs 0.2), the FBIN point at the worse end of its window (33.05 or 35.57 V: FBIN over temperature and R8, R9 at 1 %),
       cells 10 K above the NOCT model, a 10 m lead (twice the loop), and the hotter cells' own loss of maximum-power energy
       (the lower of the model's and the maker's -0.42 %/K). At 40/0: TYP 0.9903, WAB 0.9103 of the tracked energy.
   1c. THE ELECTRICAL AND LOSS INPUTS (basis: MAKER, NETLIST, INFERRED from a maker's figures, DECLARED, ESTIMATE)
       NOM   nominal: VBUS20 20.000 V, U3's limit 6.2 A, U3 0.9793 (TI's reading at that bus, INFERRED), U3B 0.972 (INFERRED), stage 0.93 and front end 0.93 (DECLARED), pack charge 0.95 (INFERRED, no document), lid loops 0.030 / 0.023 Ohm (ESTIMATE), V(AK) 20 mV (MAKER typical), no standby drain
       WE    RESTATED: every term with a maker's document at its worst: VBUS20 19.146 V (the steady-state range's minimum, vbus20_range.out 6), U3's limit 6.1 A (INFERRED minimum), U3 0.9733 (the makers' maxima at that bus, INFERRED by TI's method), U3B 0.963 (INFERRED, lower bracket), V(AK) 29 mV (MAKER maximum); the lid loops at their ESTIMATE's worse end 0.045 / 0.040 Ohm; the lid's standby drain 1.8 Wh over 72 h added to the load. CONDITIONAL ON three undocumented efficiencies held at their declared values: stage 0.93, front end 0.93, pack charge 0.95
       WE60  WE with U3's limit at the 6.0 A bracket
       WEL   WE with the bus at its endurance bracket 18.782 V (the resistors at the makers' 1000 h limits; a bound)
       WA    WE60 with the three undocumented efficiencies at their brackets' lower ends: stage 0.90, front end 0.90, pack charge 0.90
       WE1   the FIRST issue's WE (V(AK), the lid loops and the drain nominal), for continuity with CHECK-1's figures
       GEN   board A AS GENERATED: R11 10 mOhm, the front end's limit 4.30 A minimum, U3's limit set under it at 4.15 A (entry E1; its 4.25 A maximum is 50 mA under the front end's minimum); bus nominal; U3 0.9810; the rest nominal
       M207  for comparison, the model as published: 20.7 V, 6.1 A, U3 0.979 and U3B 0.972 carried (plane_grid.out case P)
       SC76  for comparison, SC-76's basis: 19.08 V, 6.1 A, U3 and U3B carried (plane_grid.out case V19)
       Common to every case: 400 Wp (four Renogy RNG-100DB-H in 2S2P) into a 200 W stage window, the drafted entry (R11
       6.2 mOhm: the front end limits at 6.94 A minimum, above U3; GEN excepted), U3B at code 62 (7.936 A), PS-IDLE-SPEC 42.8 W
       at the pack terminals, the cells aged to 80 percent, the 3.00 V line with the 5 percent reserve, the charge and discharge
       split by capacity. The standby drain is carried as load at the pack terminals, split by capacity like the rest.
   1d. THE PASS LINES: M1 is MET when neither start stops the kit. The two tests beside it, each against the floor 4.2 Wh,
       the model's hourly-step sensitivity as reconcile_lid_panel.out's NOTES print it (measured at 40/0 at an earlier
       issue's settings; CHECK-1 measured at most 0.1 Wh at WE): COMBINED, the lowest store of both packs together above it;
       EACH PACK, the base's and the lid's own lowest stores each above it (a pack at 0.0 Wh has reached its own 3.00 V
       line with the reserve: the kit runs on on the other pack). Which one REQ-072 needs is the owner's reading: L3-OD1's
       drafted ruling on fnd/l3r2 reads 'the pack' in a requirement as each pack unless it names one.

2. THE THREE UNDOCUMENTED EFFICIENCIES: WHAT THE MAKERS' OWN DOCUMENTS GIVE
   board E's stage (LT8705A, declared 0.93, bracket 0.90 to 0.97, 'NOT PLOTTED at this ratio'): 8705af p.41's own 12 V, 15 A
      design (the same M1 and M2 parts as board E's Q3 and Q4) reads 96.5 to 96.8 % at 6 to 12 A from 35 V (TYPICAL, 25 C, INFERRED;
      curve_readings.out 2). Not a figure for board E at 34.3 to 15.1 V over the day's hours: NOT ESTABLISHED.
   board A's front end (LM5176, declared 0.93, bracket 0.90 to 0.97, 'NOT PLOTTED at 20 V out'): SNVSAI1D p.9 Figure 6-2's
      9 V to 12 V boost reads 97.8 to 97.9 % at 5.5 to 6 A (TYPICAL, 25 C, INFERRED; curve_readings.out 1). Not a figure for
      board A at 15.1 to 20 V, 200 kHz, 10 uH: NOT ESTABLISHED.
   the pack's charge efficiency (declared 0.95, bracket 0.90 to 0.98, energy_inputs.yaml 'INFERRED ... no held document gives
      it'): Samsung SDI's INR18650-35E sheet (v2/vendor/battery/samsung-35e-conrad.pdf, pinned by energy_inputs.yaml) gives p.3 the standard 0.2C discharge,
      3.482 Ah and 12.62 Wh (a mean 3.624 V), and p.7 one storage sample's initial AC-IR 19.8 mOhm and DC-IR 34.5 mOhm. It gives no
      charged energy, charge curve, coulombic efficiency or hysteresis. The resistive part alone, (OCV - I_dis R) / (OCV + I_chg R)
      with OCV 3.648 V (the 0.2C mean plus its own IR drop) and R the sample's DC-IR (INFERRED):
         base 4S6P at U3's 3.968 A          0.661 A a cell charging, 0.246 A discharging: 0.9915
         lid 4S14P at U3B's 7.936 A         0.567 A a cell charging, 0.148 A discharging: 0.9933
         lid 4S15P at U3B's 7.936 A         0.529 A a cell charging, 0.141 A discharging: 0.9937
      That is an UPPER bound on the charge efficiency (the undocumented losses only lower it): NOT ESTABLISHED.

